@reduz You have a point. However, it is never good to have skew in Gizmo as a result of using skinning.

Currently, gizmo uses ArrayMesh, so if we use ImmediateMesh, we can expect some performance improvement, but we will probably need to change not only skeleton but all child class of Node3D gizmo at the same time.

Also, the SkeletonGizmo is only redrawn when tools is true, so there is no need to worry about performance in general games.

